From: FlyCat local customization
Subject: [PATCH] tunnel/statistic: add event-driven traffic push & idle dormancy ticker

Add OnJoin/OnLeave/OnTrafficUpdate callbacks to Manager for real-time
traffic statistics push to the Android layer, and replace the always-on
1s statistics ticker with the wake/dormancy ticker from the eBPF
channel's power work: handle() sleeps while idle and is re-armed by
wakeTraffic() when traffic arrives, so idle periods produce no wakeups.
Pushes ride the same tick -- fired when traffic flowed or the rate
changed, including the drop to zero before dormancy -- and lastPushed*
are atomic.

Rate-limit updateMemory to one shared RSS sample per second behind a
mutex and switch the memory field to atomic.Uint64, so dashboard
polling stops re-sampling RSS per request.

Add InitialUpload/InitialDownload fields to TrackerInfo so consumers
can compute per-connection traffic deltas without maintaining external
baselines (B1 design: delta at source); the touched literals are gofmt
aligned like the eBPF variant.

This single patch supersedes the former separate idle-dormancy patch:
the two were an atomic unit (0004's pre-image was 0002's post-image).
Not needed on the eBPF channel, whose upstream already carries the
dormancy design.
